      "funding_type": "grant",
      "typical_award_size": "Richmond does not run its own CDBG or HOME program. The adopted Housing Element states that although Richmond is eligible to be a HUD entitlement city, after staffing cuts the City opted for Contra Costa County to receive its share of HUD funding, and that the County administers CDBG and HOME for Richmond; the County CDBG page defines the Urban County as the entire county less Antioch, Concord, Pittsburg and Walnut Creek, so Richmond is inside the Urban County and the County HOME Consortium. The Housing Element cites the CDBG-assisted rehabilitation of the 150-unit Hacienda Apartments. The Richmond Housing Authority no longer administers vouchers: the County administers the Housing Choice Voucher program (about 1,700 vouchers used in Richmond, including project-based vouchers), and Miraflores received 79 RHA project-based vouchers earlier. The 2015 HUD figure of $1,092,323 predates the switch and should not be used.",
      "per_unit_cap": "None published.",
